; Al. proton-13. period 3, group 13. valence: 3.
; most abundant metal in earth's crust. lightweight. corrosion-resistant (Al2O3 layer).
; forms alloys with Mg, Cu, Si — used in aircraft, packaging, construction.
; excellent electrical conductor (used in high-voltage power lines).
; amphoteric: reacts with both acids and bases.
; Al2O3 (alumina): corundum — ruby and sapphire are alumina with trace metals.

